  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Starting at 2nd level, a cartomancer gains a pool of fate points, which measures her capacity to follow and manipulate the skeins of fate. Given this sort of work requires actual understanding of how the world works rather than sheer force of will, the number of points in a cartomancer's fate pool is equal to 1/2 her cartomancer level + herWisdom modifier.</p>\n<p>Whenever a cartomancer spends fate points, roll once on <strong>Table: Tell Fortune Outcomes</strong> for each fate point expended. On a result of a natural '1', '13', or '20', roll again as if the cartomancer is giving herself a bad fortune using the tell fortune class feature. The penalty, or, if lucky, the benefit, lasts for minutes equal to the cartomancer's class level. The heightened fate class feature applies.</p>\n<p>By spending 1 point from her fate pool, a cartomancer can do one of the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Play a least portent as a move action, but only if she cast a lesser or greater portent in the same round, or</li>\n<li>Play a lesser portent as a move action, but only if she cast a greater portent in the same round, or</li>\n<li>Draw a card as a swift action, or</li>\n<li>Reveal the top three cards of your active deck, then put them back on top of your deck in any order. This is a standard action.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/cartomancer#toc10\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
